From: NickLabs Orbis <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/ps4_bridge: advertise only 1080p60 (CEA VIC 16)

ps4_bridge_get_modes() offers both 1920x1080@60 (VIC 16, preferred) and
1920x1080@120 (VIC 63). Display managers and compositors have been observed
to select the 120 Hz mode on 60 Hz panels, leaving the HDMI output black
(aday1/ps4-hdmi-blackscreen, DionKill/ps4-linux-tutorial issues.md).

Advertise only VIC 16, and return the number of modes added (1) instead of 0
so probe helpers do not treat the connector as mode-less.

Ported from Linux psX 0011-amdgpu-ps4-bridge-remove-1080p120-mode.patch
(meerzulee/linux-psx, platforms/ps4/patches/6.18-baikal/0300-gpu-liverpool),
which does not apply to the 6.15.4 crashnt tree. The mode_1080p120 table
entry is kept (now unused, __maybe_unused) so mode_valid() is unchanged.

Status: compile-tested only (see docs/RELEASE-STATUS.md). Not boot-tested.

License: GPL-2.0 (kernel)
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
index 925986f..c133861 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/ps4_bridge.c
@@ -718,7 +718,7 @@ static const struct drm_display_mode mode_1080p = {
  * Try setting a TYPE_PREFFERED mode
  */
 /* 63 - 1920x1080@120Hz */
-static const struct drm_display_mode mode_1080p120 = {
+static const struct drm_display_mode mode_1080p120 __maybe_unused = {
 	DRM_MODE("1920x1080", DRM_MODE_TYPE_DRIVER, 297000, 1920, 2008,
 			2052, 2200, 0, 1080, 1084, 1089, 1125, 0,
 		   DRM_MODE_FLAG_PHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_PVSYNC),
@@ -732,10 +732,16 @@ int ps4_bridge_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 	pr_debug("ps4_bridge_get_modes\n");
 
 	newmode = drm_mode_duplicate(dev, &mode_1080p);
+	if (!newmode)
+		return 0;
 	drm_mode_probed_add(connector, newmode);
 
-	newmode = drm_mode_duplicate(dev, &mode_1080p120);
-	drm_mode_probed_add(connector, newmode);
+	/*
+	 * Orbis: do not advertise CEA VIC 63 (1080p120). Display managers and
+	 * compositors pick it on 60 Hz panels, which blanks the output. The
+	 * mode table entry stays so mode_valid() behaviour is unchanged for
+	 * clients that request it explicitly.
+	 */
 
 	//newmode = drm_mode_duplicate(dev, &mode_720p);
 	//drm_mode_probed_add(connector, newmode);
@@ -744,7 +750,7 @@ int ps4_bridge_get_modes(struct drm_connector *connector)
 
 	drm_connector_update_edid_property(connector, NULL);
 
-	return 0;
+	return 1;
 }
 
 enum drm_connector_status ps4_bridge_detect(struct drm_connector *connector,
